HandEmptyAfterPosting = off

Did you drop your millisecond timer in the empty hole?

Did you give the box to the robot?

Did you train the robot to copy the 1 and drop it on the 3?

And did you train the robot to copy the 1,000 and drop it on the 2,999?

Did you use Dusty to erase the first number, the 3, and 2,999 from the robot's thought bubble?

Did you flip the 3 over and put the robot and box on the back?

Did you flip the number back over and set it down to watch it work?

Well, here's what I would do if I could get around.  I'd drop the
millisecond timer in the first hole of the box.  Then I'd give the
box to the robot. And train him to copy the 1 and drop it on the 3 to
keep track of seconds. And I'd train him to copy the 1,000 and drop it on the 2,999
to keep track of milliseconds.  Then I'd erase all the numbers from the
robot's thought bubble.  I'd flip the 3 over by pressing 'f' and put
the robot on the back.  Then I'd give the robot the box and pick up
the number and flip it back over.  I'd set it down to watch it work
and then pick it up.
